{"id":"C-002","found":"2026-08-09","summary":"a post-merge retraction is refused by the counter, not by the epoch pin","diagnosis":"THE DOCUMENT WAS WRONG. 0104_fn_disposition_retract_only.sql's header claims 23503 on epoch_pin_permit. The trigger's own UPDATE moves open_blocking and gate_epoch together, and the subject row's CHECK is evaluated before its composite foreign key, so gate_closed_when_issued fires and the pin never runs. Depth 2 either way; the exhibit is the counter's.","steps":[{"op":"create_subject","subject":0,"expect":"accept"},{"op":"materialise_check","subject":0,"check":0,"expect":"accept"},{"op":"sign_disposition","check":0,"disposition":0,"expect":"accept"},{"op":"create_subject","subject":1,"expect":"accept"},{"op":"materialise_check","subject":1,"check":1,"expect":"accept"},{"op":"sign_disposition","check":1,"disposition":1,"expect":"accept"},{"op":"attempt_merge","subject":0,"expect":"accept"},{"op":"retract","disposition":0,"by":1,"expect":["23514","gate_closed_when_issued"]},{"op":"suspend","subject":0,"expect":"accept"},{"op":"retract","disposition":0,"by":1,"expect":["23503","epoch_pin_permit"]}]}
{"id":"C-003","found":"2026-08-09","summary":"a retraction naming a disposition whose INSERT was refused","diagnosis":"THE MODEL WAS WRONG. A refused sign_disposition still put its id into the Hypothesis bundle, so a later retract named it as the RETRACTOR. The cluster refused with 23503 on disposition_retracted_by_fkey; the oracle predicted Accept because it had no notion that retracted_by must reference a row that exists. Fixed by the fifth branch of Model.retract.","steps":[{"op":"create_subject","subject":0,"expect":"accept"},{"op":"materialise_check","subject":0,"check":0,"expect":"accept"},{"op":"expire_override","check":0,"disposition":0,"expect":"accept"},{"op":"sign_disposition","check":0,"disposition":1,"expect":["23505","one_live_disposition"]},{"op":"materialise_check","subject":0,"check":1,"expect":"accept"},{"op":"expire_override","check":1,"disposition":2,"expect":"accept"},{"op":"retract","disposition":2,"by":1,"expect":["23503","disposition_retracted_by_fkey"]}]}
{"id":"C-004","found":"2026-08-09","summary":"expiry does not free the one_live_disposition slot","diagnosis":"THE MODEL WAS WRONG. The oracle treated 'covered' and 'occupies the slot' as one predicate. one_live_disposition is a partial unique index over retracted_by IS NULL, so an expired verdict still HOLDS the slot while it has stopped COVERING the obligation. Signing over it is 23505; clearing the obligation needs a retraction first. Fixed by splitting _Obligation.live from _covered().","steps":[{"op":"create_subject","subject":0,"expect":"accept"},{"op":"materialise_check","subject":0,"check":0,"expect":"accept"},{"op":"expire_override","check":0,"disposition":0,"expect":"accept"},{"op":"sign_disposition","check":0,"disposition":1,"expect":["23505","one_live_disposition"]},{"op":"attempt_merge","subject":0,"expect":["P0001","trappoint_ref.fn_permit_merge_gate"]}]}
{"id":"C-005","found":"2026-08-09","summary":"CF-01 in miniature: the projected counter is the only thing between an open obligation and a merge","diagnosis":"NOT A DEFECT — the canonical admitted-then-refused history, recorded so a regression in either direction is caught by a fixed expectation rather than by agreement. An obligation arriving after clearance leaves the subject in `dispositioned`, so the legal edge to `merged` exists and only gate_closed_when_issued stands between the write and a merged permit carrying an open precursor.","steps":[{"op":"create_subject","subject":0,"expect":"accept"},{"op":"materialise_check","subject":0,"check":0,"expect":"accept"},{"op":"sign_disposition","check":0,"disposition":0,"expect":"accept"},{"op":"materialise_check","subject":0,"check":1,"expect":"accept"},{"op":"attempt_merge","subject":0,"expect":["23514","gate_closed_when_issued"]},{"op":"sign_disposition","check":1,"disposition":1,"expect":"accept"},{"op":"attempt_merge","subject":0,"expect":"accept"},{"op":"materialise_check","subject":0,"check":2,"expect":["P0001","trappoint_ref.fn_check_materialised"]},{"op":"attempt_merge","subject":0,"expect":["23503","legal_edge"]}]}
